1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Be2 O-O 6. f4 c5 7. d5 e6 8. Nf3 exd5
9. e5 Nfd7 10. cxd5 dxe5 11. O-O exf4 12. Bxf4 Qb6 13. Qd2 Nf6 14. Ne5 Nbd7 15.
Nc4 Qd8 16. a4 a6 {(This move is important in lines where the BR goes to e8 as
otherwise White would have an obvious Bb5 skewer)} {JS reconstruction up to
move 21} 17. Bd6 Re8 18. Rad1 Nb6 ({Stockfish gives} 18... b5 $1 {winning but
the players could be forgiven for missing it}) 19. Qf4 {(This move has to
happen as otherwise there is no way the d6 bishop can sensibly go to c7)} Nxc4
20. Bxc4 Bf5 21. Bc7 Qd7 22. d6 Ng4 23. Nd5 Be5 24. Qg5 Bxh2+ 25. Kh1 Bxd6 26.
Ba5 h6 {(Big blunder but maybe Black was in time trouble)} 27. Qxg4 Bxg4 28.
Nf6+ Kg7 29. Nxd7 Bxd1 30. Rxf7+ Kh8 31. Bc3+ {source: bulletin 
(reconstruction & comments JS, also AA)} 1-0

